{"4867400": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Chronicles of Ilseera: Tarrowmorr", "steam_appid": 4867400, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "dlc": [4965830], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Long forgotten, and isolated from the rest of<i> Ilseera</i>, delve into the isolated fantastical island of<strong><i> Tarrowmorr</i></strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On this adventure, you play as <i>Kayleigh</i>, a pirate trying to escape from her past who winds up marooned on a strange island not found on the maps. While searching for your crew-mates, you find yourself becoming entwined in the very fate of the residents of Tarrowmorr. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will Kayleigh continue to run, or will she discover what it means to truly become a Hero...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Designed to look and feel like a video game that could have come out in the late 1990s, Tarrowmorr embraces the design ethos present in a lot of video games from that time. Low-poly models with low-res textures and smaller, handcrafted level spaces to explore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Tarrowmorr, you spend your time exploring the strange island and helping the people you find along the way. The core game-play loop involves: </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Questing and Helping the People you encounter</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Delving into dungeons</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fighting various <i>Monsters </i>and<i> Enemies</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Using the items you find to progress further in your journey</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Discovering Secrets and finding collectables throughout the island</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you delve deeper into the island, the stakes increase and the story gets darker. A linear and story driven adventure awaits you on the Island of<i> Tarrowmorr</i>...</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Long forgotten, and isolated from the rest of<i> Ilseera</i>, delve into the isolated fantastical island of<strong><i> Tarrowmorr</i></strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On this adventure, you play as <i>Kayleigh</i>, a pirate trying to escape from her past who winds up marooned on a strange island not found on the maps. While searching for your crew-mates, you find yourself becoming entwined in the very fate of the residents of Tarrowmorr. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will Kayleigh continue to run, or will she discover what it means to truly become a Hero...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Designed to look and feel like a video game that could have come out in the late 1990s, Tarrowmorr embraces the design ethos present in a lot of video games from that time. Low-poly models with low-res textures and smaller, handcrafted level spaces to explore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Tarrowmorr, you spend your time exploring the strange island and helping the people you find along the way. The core game-play loop involves: </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Questing and Helping the People you encounter</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Delving into dungeons</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fighting various <i>Monsters </i>and<i> Enemies</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Using the items you find to progress further in your journey</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Discovering Secrets and finding collectables throughout the island</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you delve deeper into the island, the stakes increase and the story gets darker. A linear and story driven adventure awaits you on the Island of<i> Tarrowmorr</i>...</p>", "short_description": "Delve into a Fantasy land with Dinosaurs, Magic, and Kingdoms at the edge of war. Explore the island of Tarrowmorr in this retro style, action adventure game designed to look and feel as though it was made in the late 1990s.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4867400/4a93c0293860e8fdfcf726da551a22ad647a177e/header.jpg?t=1784861506", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4867400/98a3b22c43cac58614c7951d62ec606ce07ad418/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1784861506", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4867400/98a3b22c43cac58614c7951d62ec606ce07ad418/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1784861506", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Direct3D 12 Compatible Graphics Card<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 2 GB available space</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": [], "linux_requirements": [], "developers": ["ButFishButGames"], "publishers": ["ButFishButGames"], "demos": [{"appid": 4965830, "description": ""}], "package_groups": [], "platforms": {"windows": true, "mac": false, "linux": false}, "categories": [{"id": 2, "description": "Single-player"}, {"id": 28, "description": "Full controller support"}, {"id": 68, "description": "Custom Volume Controls"}, {"id": 60, "description": "Gamepad Recommended"}, {"id": 55, "description": "DualShock Controller Support"}, {"id": 79, "description": "Save Anytime"}, {"id": 69, "description": "Stereo Sound"}, {"id": 62, "description": "Family Sharing"}], "genres": [{"id": "1", "description": "Action"}, {"id": "25", "descriptio